replace the GBA colour correction with Switch Online's

This changes how GBA games look rather than making upstream work here.
The Color Correction setting is unchanged in the menu and in
slot_state.txt, but for a GBA cart "on" now means the filter in
libretro's NSO-gba-color.slang (sRGB profile), which is
gentler than mGBA's and gpSP's own correction: it keeps primaries
saturated where theirs bleed them into each other, so yellows stay
yellow rather than turning salmon. Game Boy and Game Boy Color carts
are untouched.

The filter runs in the software compositor's frame upload, before the
LCD3x mask. A GBA frame is 5 bits a channel, so it is a 32,768-entry
table built the first time it is wanted and one lookup a pixel after
that, costing upload_us in the SLOT_TRACE_LATENCY profile and nothing
elsewhere. colour_option now holds both cores' own GBA correction off
whatever the setting says, or the colours would be corrected twice.

The GL compositor has no equivalent, so a desktop host build shows GBA
games uncorrected. This port runs the software backend.
